{"vid":"pEO9-iPZQWA","source":"pEO9-iPZQWA.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":7.7,"txt":"Hello. This is 6 Minute English from BBC Learning English."},{"t":11.4,"txt":"I'm Phil."},{"t":12.4,"txt":"It seems that we're hearing about more and more terrible weather events,"},{"t":16.4,"txt":"but how exactly is climate change affecting extreme weather?"},{"t":20.3,"txt":"I'm lucky today to be joined by BBC weather forecaster, meteorologist"},{"t":24.4,"txt":"and presenter Sarah Keith-Lucas. Hi, Sarah."},{"t":27.3,"txt":"Hi, Phil, it's great to be here."},{"t":29,"txt":"Sarah is here to help us understand what's happening with extreme weather."},{"t":33.1,"txt":"She'll also help explain some of the words and expressions used"},{"t":36.8,"txt":"in a new series of BBC Learning English videos, all about weather and climate,"},{"t":41.3,"txt":"and the language we use to talk about them."},{"t":43.1,"txt":"You can find the link to them"},{"t":44.3,"txt":"on our web page or in the show notes for this podcast."},{"t":47.1,"txt":"Sarah, let's start with a really important question."},{"t":50.5,"txt":"What's the difference between climate and weather?"},{"t":54.3,"txt":"That's a great question, Phil."},{"t":56.1,"txt":"The weather is what you see and feel every day."},{"t":59.7,"txt":"Climate is more long term."},{"t":61.8,"txt":"Today, I'll explain how a change in the climate"},{"t":64.6,"txt":"over the long term can be seen in the weather that we experience."},{"t":68.7,"txt":"And as always,"},{"t":69.9,"txt":"we'll also be learning some key vocabulary to talk about the topic."},{"t":73.4,"txt":"And Sarah, it's traditional for us to set a quiz question."},{"t":77,"txt":"Have you got one for us? Yes I have."},{"t":79.5,"txt":"By how much has the Earth's temperature increased since 1970?"},{"t":84.5,"txt":"Is it a) around 0.5C?"},{"t":88.5,"txt":"b) around 1C or c) around 2C?"},{"t":94,"txt":"Erm, around 2C?"},{"t":95.9,"txt":"I'll give you the answer at the end of the programme,"},{"t":98.2,"txt":"so listen to the end to find out."},{"t":100.5,"txt":"Now we're going to talk about tropical storms."},{"t":104.1,"txt":"What do we mean by tropical storms, Sarah?"},{"t":107.2,"txt":"Well those are hurricanes, cyclones and typhoons."},{"t":111,"txt":"They're large rotating storms formed over warm tropical waters."},{"t":116,"txt":"They're actually the same."},{"t":117.7,"txt":"We just use different names depending on where in the world they form."},{"t":122,"txt":"Hurricanes in the Atlantic."},{"t":124,"txt":"Cyclones in the Indian Ocean and typhoons in the West Pacific."},{"t":128.9,"txt":"As the world warms,"},{"t":130.3,"txt":"climate scientists think that these storms will get more destructive."},{"t":134.4,"txt":"In one of our new learning English for weather videos."},{"t":137.9,"txt":"Meteorologist Darren Bett tells us about another worrying change."},{"t":143,"txt":"Scientists also think storms are slowing down."},{"t":146.9,"txt":"They're not moving across as quickly."},{"t":149,"txt":"And that means if a storm is in the same area for longer,"},{"t":153.5,"txt":"the winds will be stronger for longer and the rain will last for longer,"},{"t":158,"txt":"producing more flooding and more likelihood of flooding and landslides"},{"t":163.4,"txt":"and also mudslides."},{"t":165.1,"txt":"Darren said that if a storm moves more slowly,"},{"t":168.6,"txt":"there will be more likelihood of flooding."},{"t":171.3,"txt":"'Likelihood' is the noun that we use to say how probable"},{"t":174.7,"txt":"or how likely something is to happen."},{"t":177.6,"txt":"Darren also told us about landslides and mudslides."},{"t":181.8,"txt":"Yes, landslides are where a large amount of earth"},{"t":185.3,"txt":"or rock moves down a slope quickly."},{"t":188.3,"txt":"Mudslides tend to be faster and more liquid."},{"t":192.2,"txt":"Both of these things can happen after particularly heavy rain"},{"t":196.4,"txt":"and can cause damage to buildings."},{"t":199.1,"txt":"People can also be killed or injured by them."},{"t":202.3,"txt":"What else causes loss of life in a hurricane, typhoon, or cyclone?"},{"t":206.4,"txt":"Well, something else that is very dangerous is a storm surge."},{"t":210.3,"txt":"Let's hear again from my colleague Darren Bett."},{"t":213.2,"txt":"Storm surge."},{"t":214.2,"txt":"That's that body of water that gets swept inland"},{"t":217.2,"txt":"and produces widespread flooding."},{"t":219.9,"txt":"Climate change is warming our seas and the sea levels are rising."},{"t":225.6,"txt":"That potentially could mean that storm surge, which is one element"},{"t":231.2,"txt":"of a storm that produces more casualties than any other."},{"t":235.3,"txt":"Those storm surges could become even more dangerous."},{"t":239.6,"txt":"So, we had the word 'casualty',"},{"t":242.2,"txt":"and this is used to talk about people killed or injured by an accident,"},{"t":246.3,"txt":"a military attack, or in this case, an extreme weather event."},{"t":249.6,"txt":"Darren talked about storm surges."},{"t":252.6,"txt":"A storm surge is where the sea level rises quickly,"},{"t":256.4,"txt":"pushed by strong winds caused by a storm."},{"t":259.9,"txt":"This water comes onto land with an enormous amount of force,"},{"t":264.1,"txt":"and storm surges can be up to ten metres high."},{"t":267.9,"txt":"Buildings get destroyed and people can drown."},{"t":271,"txt":"We heard about the storm sweeping inland."},{"t":273.9,"txt":"Something sweeping in is moving quickly and powerfully,"},{"t":277.8,"txt":"and you can hear more from Darren in the videos on our website."},{"t":281.2,"txt":"Sarah, how about the answer to the quiz question you asked earlier?"},{"t":285,"txt":"OK, Phil. So I asked by"},{"t":287.4,"txt":"how much has the world's average temperature increased since 1970?"},{"t":292.2,"txt":"And I thought it was around 2C."},{"t":295.6,"txt":"It's actually around 1C."},{"t":298.7,"txt":"1C is just an average across all of Earth's land and ocean surface."},{"t":303.7,"txt":"Some places are warming much quicker than this, such as the Arctic."},{"t":307.6,"txt":"That's warming three times faster than the average rate,"},{"t":310.7,"txt":"just a small increase in average temperature can lead to"},{"t":313.7,"txt":"a much bigger increase in extreme events such as heatwaves, wildfires and floods."},{"t":319.8,"txt":"Wow. So that is an important difference."},{"t":322.4,"txt":"OK, let's recap the vocabulary we've learned starting with 'likelihood',"},{"t":327.2,"txt":"which is the noun that we use to talk about how probable"},{"t":330.4,"txt":"or how likely something is to happen."},{"t":332.8,"txt":"Landslides and mudslides, which can occur after heavy rainfall,"},{"t":337.4,"txt":"make earth or mud move downhill very fast."},{"t":341.6,"txt":"A storm surge is a sudden rise in the sea level that can move inland,"},{"t":346,"txt":"causing destruction."},{"t":347.4,"txt":"If something sweeps in, it moves in very fast and very powerfully."},{"t":352.7,"txt":"And finally, a casualty is someone who is injured"},{"t":356.1,"txt":"or killed by an accident, attack,"},{"t":358.4,"txt":"or something like an extreme weather event. Once again our six minutes are up."},{"t":363,"txt":"Goodbye. Thanks for joining us today,"},{"t":364.7,"txt":"Sarah! Bye!"}],"words":[{"t":7.68,"w":"Hello."},{"t":7.68,"w":"This"},{"t":7.68,"w":"is"},{"t":7.68,"w":"6"},{"t":7.68,"w":"Minute"},{"t":7.68,"w":"English"},{"t":7.68,"w":"from"},{"t":7.68,"w":"BBC"},{"t":7.68,"w":"Learning"},{"t":7.68,"w":"English."},{"t":11.4,"w":"I'm"},{"t":11.4,"w":"Phil."},{"t":12.4,"w":"It"},{"t":12.4,"w":"seems"},{"t":12.4,"w":"that"},{"t":12.4,"w":"we're"},{"t":12.4,"w":"hearing"},{"t":12.4,"w":"about"},{"t":12.4,"w":"more"},{"t":12.4,"w":"and"},{"t":12.4,"w":"more"},{"t":12.4,"w":"terrible"},{"t":12.4,"w":"weather"},{"t":12.4,"w":"events,"},{"t":16.44,"w":"but"},{"t":16.44,"w":"how"},{"t":16.44,"w":"exactly"},{"t":16.44,"w":"is"},{"t":16.44,"w":"climate"},{"t":